<title>FINLAND: FINLAND BANK SUPERVISOR CONFIRMS ERM PROPOSAL.</title>
<headline>FINLAND BANK SUPERVISOR CONFIRMS ERM PROPOSAL.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finland Bank supervisory board member Anneli Jaatteenmaki on Saturday confirmed the board had met on Friday and proposed to the government that the markka be linked to Europe's Exchange Rate Mechanism.</p>
<p>&quot;Yes, the meeting was held yesterday,&quot; she told Reuters by telephone. Asked what the central parity was, she said: &quot;It is a secret decision.&quot;</p>
</text>
